description: "How Typedown thinks about content: editor setup, vaults, documents, schemas, and deployment."
---

This section walks through setting up your editor, understanding the core concepts, and deploying a site. Each page builds on the previous one, so reading in order is recommended.

- [Editor setup](01-editor-setup): configure Neovim, VS Code, or Zed for autocompletion and type checking
- [Vault and documents](02-vault-and-documents): the project structure, file anatomy, and the content graph
- [Schemas and types](03-schemas-and-types): defining node types, field types, inheritance, expressions, and references
- [Deploying](04-deploying): build a static site and deploy it
